  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Abhay Kumar Gunjan vs The State Of Jharkhand .... .... .... ... on 16 June, 2021",
    "facts": "Apprehending his arrest in connection with Argora P.S. Case No.186 of 2020 instituted under Sections 273/34 of the Indian Penal Code read with Section 59 (iii) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, the petitioner has moved this Court for grant of privileges of anticipatory bail.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the co-accused Ishan is the distributor of Pan Masala in the name of his firm namely Vivaan Enterprises having license issued by the Government of India and the petitioner has been implicated in this case only because he is the younger brother of the co-accused- Ishan and the allegation against the petitioner is that he was also selling illegal tobacco products in collusion with the co-accused. It is submitted that the allegation against the petitioner is false. It is further submitted that the co-accused- Ishan has already been given the privileges of anticipatory bail by a co-ordinate Bench of this Court vide order dated 01.03.2021 passed in A.B.A. No.6411 of 2020. It is lastly submitted that the petitioner is ready and willing to co-operate with the investigation of the case. Hence, it is submitted that the petitioner be given the privileges of anticipatory bail. Learned P.P appearing for the State opposes the prayer for anticipatory bail of the petitioner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the co-accused Ishan is the distributor of Pan Masala in the name of his firm namely Vivaan Enterprises having license issued by the Government of India and the petitioner has been implicated in this case only because he is the younger brother of the co-accused- Ishan and the allegation against the petitioner is that he was also selling illegal tobacco products in collusion with the co-accused. It is submitted that the allegation against the petitioner is false. It is further submitted that the co-accused- Ishan has already been given the privileges of anticipatory bail by a co-ordinate Bench of this Court vide order dated 01.03.2021 passed in A.B.A. No.6411 of 2020. It is lastly submitted that the petitioner is ready and willing to co-operate with the investigation of the case. Hence, it is submitted that the petitioner be given the privileges of anticipatory bail. Learned P.P appearing for the State opposes the prayer for anticipatory bail of the petitioner.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
